    {
      "id": "p0251-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The localization team easily fixed the first two issues. The third issue came into play a year after Undertale's Japanese release, when the game's official soundtrack was set to be released in Japan. Because this track is so iconic and memorable, Toby requested that the Japanese soundtrack retain the \"SAVE the World\" name as-is rather than replace it with a less memorable pun onfukkatsl.1.",
        "raw": "The localization team easily fixed the first two issues. The third issue came\ninto play a year after Undertale's Japanese release, when the game's official\nsoundtrack was set to be released in Japan. Because this track is so iconic and\nmemorable, Toby requested that the Japanese soundtrack retain the \"SAVE the\nWorld\" name as-is rather than replace it with a less memorable pun onfukkatsl.1.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.0937609,
          0.49799286,
          0.70325248,
          0.5841
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09031538,
          0.49727857,
          0.70528524,
          0.58517143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          20,
          21,
          22,
          23,
          24
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "前两个问题很容易解决。第三个问题，则在《Undertale》日版推出一年后、官方原声带准备在日本发行时显现出来。因为这首曲子太有代表性、太令人难忘，Toby 要求日版原声带原样保留“SAVE the World”，不要换成一个不如原名好记的 fukkatsu 双关。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
